readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Linuxi3a	Linuxi3a			0	om	There is a wide variety of Linux distributions, and even within the same distribution there may be different installation options (KDE vs Gnome, etc.). Some distributions ship with their own ‘native’ version of ${PRODUCTNAME}, which may have different features from this Community ${PRODUCTNAME}. Sometimes you can install the Community ${PRODUCTNAME} alongside the ‘native’ version. However, it’s usually safer to remove the ‘native’ version before installing this Community version. Consult the documentation for your distribution for details of how to do this.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Linuxi4a	Linuxi4a			0	om	Mosajjii ijaaruun ykn balleessuun dura dilbii sirna keetii yeroo baay'ee akka fudhattu gorfamta				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Precautions	Precautions			0	om	Sirna keerratti galeeloo ammaafii keessaa kuufannoo duwwaa gahaa akka qabduu fi mirgoonni gahiinsaa dubbisuu, barreessuu fi kaasuu akka siif laataman mirkaneeffadhu. Ijaarsa kaasuun dura sagantaalee biroo mara cufi.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso01	naso01			0	om	Rakkoolee Yammuu Eegala Sagantaa				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso02	naso02			0	om	If you experience ${PRODUCTNAME} startup problems (most notably while using Gnome) please 'unset' the <tt>SESSION_MANAGER</tt> environment variable inside the shell you use to start ${PRODUCTNAME}. This can be done by adding the line "<tt>unset SESSION_MANAGER</tt>" to the beginning of the soffice shell script found in the "<tt>[office folder]/program</tt>" directory.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	abcdef	abcdef			0	om	Ulfeenyi ${PRODUCTNAME} kaasuu (fkn. fayyadamoonni rarra'uu) fi rakkooleen agarsiisaa ooftuu kaardii saxaatootiin dhufu. Rakkooleen kun kan mudatan taanaan, ooftuu kaardii saxaatoo kee haaromsi ykn ooftuu saxaatoo sirna dalagaa kee waliin laatame fayyadamuu yaali. Rakkooleen wantoota G3 agarsiisuu kan hiikamu 'Meeshaalee - Dirqalaalee - ${PRODUCTNAME} - Mul'isi - Mul'annoo G3' jalatti dirqala "Use OpenGL" kaka'umsaleessuudhaani.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso	naso			0	om	Ganaatuqeewwan yaadannoo ALPS/Synaptics Wiindoo keessaa				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso2	naso2			0	om	Sababii dhimma ooftuu Wiindoo ta'eetiin, yammuu quba kee ganaatuqee ALPS/Synaptics irra mucuceessitu galmeelee ${PRODUCTNAME} keessa marsuu hin dandeessu.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso6	naso6			0	om	Marsa ganaatuqee dandeessisuuf, faayilii qindaa'inaa "<tt>C:\Program Files\Synaptics\SynTP\SynTPEnh.ini</tt>" keessatti sararoota armaan gadii dabaliitii kompiyuutara kee lamkaasi:				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso8	naso8			0	om	Yaadannoo: Iddoon faayilii qindaa'inaa fooyya'oota Wiindoo addaa addaa irratti gargar tahuu danda'a.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	sdfsd32asrc	sdfsd32asrc			0	om	Ooftuu Yaadannoo Teessoo Mooziillaa				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	sdcc32asrc	sdcc32asrc			0	om	Ooftuun yaadannoo teessoo Mooziillaa qarqaba <tt>SUNWzlib</tt> barbaada. Qarqabni kun ijaarsa  sirna dalagaa Solaariis isa gadaantoo keessa hin jiru. Gahiinsa yaadannoo teessoo Mooziillaa yoo barbaadde, qarqaba kana sirna dalagaa Solaariis keetitti ajaja "<tt>pkgadd</tt>" dhaan fayyadamuun CD ijaarsaa irraa dabali.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	awe1	awe1			0	om	Furtuulee Qaxxaamuraa				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	w32e1	w32e1			0	om	${PRODUCTNAME} keessatti furtuuleen fayyaduumuu danda'aman furtuulee qaxxaamuraa (idaatiiwwan furtuu) sirna dalagaatiin hin fayydamne qofaadha. Idaatiin furtuu ${PRODUCTNAME} keessaa akka Gargaarsa ${PRODUCTNAME} keessatti ibsameetti kan hin hojjanne yoo tahe, qaxxaamurri sun sirna dalagaatiin akka fayyadamaa jiru mirkaneeffadhu. Walitti bu'iinsa akkanaa balleessuuf, furtuulee sirna dalagaa keetiin ramadaman jijjiiruu ni dandeessa. Yookiin ammoo, ramaddii furtuu ${PRODUCTNAME} keessaa kamiyyuu jijjiiruu ni dandeessa. Odeeffannoo dabalataa dhimma kanaafiif, Gargaarsa ${PRODUCTNAME} ykn galmee Gargaarsaa sirna dalagaa keetii ilaali.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	mackeys1	mackeys1			0	om	Fayyadamni gargaarsa ${PRODUCTNAME} idaatiilee qaxxaamuraa gabatee cuqoo PC qofa fayyadamuu ni danda'a.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gfh6w	gfh6w			0	om	Saamsuu Faayilii				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76w	pji76w			0	om	File locking is enabled by default in ${PRODUCTNAME}. On a network that uses the Network File System protocol (NFS), the locking daemon for NFS clients must be active. To disable file locking, edit the <tt>soffice</tt> script and change the line "<tt>export SAL_ENABLE_FILE_LOCKING</tt>" to "<tt># export SAL_ENABLE_FILE_LOCKING</tt>". If you disable file locking, the write access of a document is not restricted to the user who first opens the document.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76wsdf	pji76wsdf			0	om	Ofeeggannoo: Amalli faayilii iggiteessuu kakaafame Solaris 2.5.1 fi 2.7 Linux NFS 2.0 waliin fayyadamu irratti rakkoo uumuu danda'a. Yoo qeeyyaan sirna kee ulaagaalee kana qabaate, amala faayilii iggiteessuu fayyadamuu akka dhiistu ciminaan si gorsina. Yoo hin taane, yammuu kompuutara Linux irratti faayilii galeeloo NFS fe'amee irraa banuuf yaaltu ${PRODUCTNAME} rarra'ee hafa.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gfh6w1	gfh6w1			0	om	Rakkoo yammuu ${PRODUCTNAME} irraa galmeewwaan akka Ergaa-etti erguu				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76w1	pji76w1			0	om	Yammuu galmee akkaataa kanaan 'Faayilii - Ergi - Galmee akka Ergaa-etti' ykn 'Galmee akka Miiltoo PDFtti' ergamu rakkoowwan uumamuu danda'u (sagantaan ni halaka ykn rarra'a). Kun sababiinsaa faayiliin sirnaa Wiindoo "Mapi" (Messaging Application Programming Interface) fooyya'oota tokko tokko keessatti rakkoo waan uumuufi. Rakkoon kun lakkoofsa fooyya'aa murtaa'etti gadi dhiphachuu hin danda'u. Odeeffannoo dabalataaf Microsoft Knowledge Base "mapi dll" barbaaduuf  <a href="https://www.microsoft.com">https://www.microsoft.com</a> doow'adhu.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	aw22	aw22			0	om	Qabanoo barbachisaa gaheenya				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	access7	access7			0	om	For more information on the accessibility features in ${PRODUCTNAME}, see <a href="https://www.openoffice.org/access/">https://www.openoffice.org/access/</a>				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	support	support			0	om	Deeggarsa Fayyadamaa				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	support1	support1			0	om	The main support page <a href="https://support.openoffice.org/">https://support.openoffice.org/</a> offers various possibilities for help with ${PRODUCTNAME}. Your question may have already been answered - check the Community Forum at <a href="https://forum.openoffice.org">https://forum.openoffice.org</a> or search the archives of the 'users@openoffice.apache.org' mailing list at <a href="https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html">https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html</a>. Alternatively, you can send in your questions to <a href="mailto:users@openoffice.apache.org">users@openoffice.apache.org</a>. How to subscribe to the list (to get an email response) is explained on this page: <a href="https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html">https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html</a>.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	faq	faq			0	om	Also check the FAQ section at <a href="https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/FAQ">https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/FAQ</a>.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	reportbugs	reportbugs			0	om	Reporting Bugs &amp; Issues				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	reportbugs1	reportbugs1			0	om	The ${PRODUCTNAME} Web site hosts <a href="https://bz.apache.org/ooo/">BugZilla</a>, our mechanism for reporting, tracking and solving bugs and issues. We encourage all users to feel entitled and welcome to report issues that may arise on your particular platform. Energetic reporting of issues is one of the most important contributions that the user community can make to the ongoing development and improvement of the suite.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettinginvolved1	gettinginvolved1			0	om	Irratti Hirmachuu				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettinginvolved2	gettinginvolved2			0	om	Hawaasni ${PRODUCTNAME} dagaagsa projektii madda banaa barbaachisaa kanarratti tattaaffiin hirmaachuu keetirraa bu'aa guddaa argata.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettingimvolved3	gettingimvolved3			0	om	As a user, you are already a valuable part of the suite's development process and we would like to encourage you to take an even more active role with a view to being a long-term contributor to the community. Please join and check out the user page at <a href="https://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html">https://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html</a>				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	howtostart	howtostart			0	om	Haala Eegalii				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	howtostart1	howtostart1			0	om	The best way to start contributing is to subscribe to one or more of the mailing lists, lurk for a while, and gradually use the mail archives to familiarize yourself with many of the topics covered since the ${PRODUCTNAME} source code was released back in October 2000. When you're comfortable, all you need to do is send an email self-introduction and jump right in.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	subscribe	subscribe			0	om	Maamiloomi				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	subscribe1	subscribe1			0	om	Here are a few of the ${PRODUCTNAME} mailing lists to which you can subscribe at <a href="https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html">https://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html</a>				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	subscribelist1	subscribelist1			0	om	News: announce@openoffice.apache.org *recommended to all users* (light traffic)				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	subscribelist2	subscribelist2			0	om	Main user forum: users@openoffice.apache.org *easy way to lurk on discussions* (heavy traffic)				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	subscribelist4	subscribelist4			0	om	General project development and discussion list: dev@openoffice.apache.org (heavy traffic)				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem					0	om	Joining the Project				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	joining	joining			0	om	Muuxannoo saxaxa mosajjii ykn lakkaddeessuu murta'aa qabaattullee proojektii madda banaa barbaachisaa kanaaf gumaacha olaanaa laachuu ni dandeessa. Eeyyee, ati!				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	joining1	joining1			0	om	At <a href="https://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html">https://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html</a> you will find a first overview where you can start with, ranging from Localization, QA, user support to some real core coding projects. If you are not a developer, you can help with Documentation or Marketing, for example. The ${PRODUCTNAME} marketing is applying both guerrilla and traditional commercial techniques to marketing open source software, and we are doing it across language and cultural barriers, so you can help just by spreading the word and telling a friend about this office suite.				20200411 15:09:53
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	joining3	joining3			0	om	You can help by joining the marketing mailing list marketing@openoffice.apache.org where you can provide point communication contact with press, media, government agencies, consultants, schools, Linux Users Groups and developers in your country and local community.				20200411 15:09:53
