helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	om	\<emph\>Dhaangessuu\</emph\>: Amala \<emph\>Dhangessuu \</emph\>qabduu \<emph\>... \</emph\>cuqaasun qaaqa\<emph\>Dhangessuu\</emph\> sarara \<emph\>Amaloota: Dirree Dhangi'e\</emph\> qindeessu dandeessa. Qaaqni \<emph\>Lakkoofsa Dhangii\</emph\> ni mul'ata.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	om	Yoo dirreen dhangi'ame gara barruu dirree kuusaa deetaatti waliindhame, galfatni dirree kana keessaa akka barrutti yaalama. yoo dirreen dhangi'ame gara dirree kuusaa deetaa akka lakkoofsatti agarsiifame waliindhame, naqni akka lakkoofsotatti yaalama. Guyyaa fi yerolleen keessaan akka lakkoofsotatti qabamu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	om	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	om	\<emph\>Gatii durtii\</emph\>: Gatiin kun akka gatii durtiitti galmee haaraaf qindeessa.				20200411 15:09:53
