helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_id7953733				0	om	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\>- Java\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Class Path\</emph\> button. After you add the path information, restart \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
