helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148462	118			0	om	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148658	119			0	om	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145371	120			0	om	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> defines the period over which an asset is depreciated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154608	121			0	om	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the length of each period. The length must be entered in the same date unit as the depreciation period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829	122			0	om	            \<emph\>Month\</emph\> (optional) denotes the number of months for the first year of depreciation. If an entry is not defined, 12 is used as the default.				20200411 15:09:53
