helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028K				0	om	SUMIFS( Reference R ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043K				0	om	Sums the value of cells in range R that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1, and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062K				0	om	A \<emph\>Criterion\</emph\> is a single cell Reference, Number or Text. If the criterion is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083K				0	om	All \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110K				0	om	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148K				0	om	Sum up cells in range A1:10 if the entries in B1:B10 are positive, and the entries in D1:D10 are the letter "A": \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIFS(A1:A10;B1:B10;">0";D1:D10;"A")\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196K				0	om	See COUNTIFS() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIFS().				20200411 15:09:53
